== Usage ==
[[File:ScaffoldingDemonstration.gif|thumb|Demonstration of the {{Item|Large Scaffolding}}]]

'''Scaffolding''', being a climbable semi-solid block, allow the player to climb up and down. They can only be used on {{Zone|Galatea}}: attempting to use '''Scaffolding''' outside of {{Zone|Galatea}} yields the following message.

{{Dialogue|&cYou must be on Galatea in order to use this item!}}

All pieces of '''Scaffolding''' inherit the {{AN|Climb!}} ability, allowing the player to place up to a certain limit: for example, the {{Item|Tiny Scaffolding}} allows the player to place {{Green|2}} Scaffolding blocks per interaction, up to {{Green|4}} Scaffolding blocks placed. Regardless of where the player physically places a Scaffolding, it will appear beneath the player.

Being more than than a certain distance from any placed '''Scaffolding''' will cause it to break. Additionally, holding Scaffolding will replace the {{Item|SkyBlock Menu}} with a {{Item|Scaffolding}} block.

'''Scaffolding''', however, has several limitations.
* Scaffolding '''cannot''' be placed horizontally.
* Scaffolding cannot be broken. In order to regain one's available Scaffolding, the player must leave its radius.
* Placing Scaffolding in an invalid position yields the following message:<br>{{Dialogue|&cYou can't place a scaffolding here!}}
* Placing Scaffolding in a location that is too low to accomodate all Scaffolding blocks yields the following message:<br>{{Dialogue|&cThere's not enough space above you to place the scaffolding!}}
* Using all of one's available Scaffolding and attempting to place more yields the following message:<br>{{Dialogue|&cYou can't use more scaffolding blocks.}}

